  "query_preview": "../Wednesday through Saturday/\nWednesday, a closed low south of the Aleutian chain will reach \nfull maturity, beginning to decay as it lifts north. Three primary\nfeatures of interest as this system moves into the Gulf are: \nstrength of the accompanying surface low, clear/warm over the \nPanhandle for the mid to end of the week, and moisture transport \ninto the region by the weekend. Touching on the low first, \nensembles show agreement that this system will make landfall along\nthe AK Peninsula, with southerlies building in the central Gulf; \nwinds remain below gale force. Our stubborn high over the eastern \nGulf cedes territory, making a slight retreat into the Panhandle, \nwith north-westerlies still impacting much of the coastal waters. \nOverall, little concern for major marine impacts with continued \nfocus for northwest winds of moderate to fresh breezes along the \nAlexander Archipelago and sea breezes thru the inside.\n\nAs this high shifts into the Panhandle Thursday, warm and dry \nonce again becomes the theme. Digging into the 850mb temps, the \nLREF shows a left-skewed distribution based around 7C to 15C, with\nthe mode around 13C, translating to 75F to 85F surface temps, \nabout 10F above normal for this time of year. The Extreme Forecast\nIndex shines more light into this, with agreement in abnormal \nwarmth increasing its footprint over the Panhandle into the end of\nthis week. A note, it\u2019s not just about the afternoon high \ntemperatures, nightly low temperatures also likely remain about \n10F above normal for most of the region. \n\nMoving onto moisture, by the end of the weekend this pattern will\nbegin to break down the dominant high, or at a minimum, push the \nridge further east, with southwesterlies picking up on some \nequatorial moisture and funneling it into the Gulf. A few ensemble\noutliers want to bring a quick hit of moderate AR conditions; \nhowever, overall modest Integrated Vapor Transport values suggest \njust an increase in clouds, and perhaps some light rain, by the \nend of the weekend.",
